= Programming with Rudiments using the unixsocketserver class =

Daemons are commonly used to serve data to clients over a network but they can also be used to serve data to processes running on the local machine.  This can be done using the inetsocketserver class but if your platform supports unix sockets, then it can be done much faster and more efficiently using the [../classes/html/classunixsocketserver.html unixsocketserver class].  The example below listens on a unix socket for a client connection, receives a string from the client, and writes a response back.

{{{#!blockquote
{{{#!code
@../../examples/unixsocketserver.cpp@
}}}
}}}

See the [unixsocketclient.html unixsocketclient] example for a client that can communicate with this server.

